From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caden-Calderon <caden.calderon03@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 18:18:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] kinect-studio: host_receive_ns stamps from parsers
 through to frames

Both stream parsers stamp CLOCK_MONOTONIC at packet completion; all
depth processors and both TurboJPEG color processors carry the stamp
onto delivered Frames. This makes capture->assembled latency honestly
measurable (E1) and feeds the frame contract's t_host_arrival.
---
 include/internal/libfreenect2/depth_packet_processor.h | 1 +
 include/internal/libfreenect2/rgb_packet_processor.h   | 1 +
 include/libfreenect2/frame_listener.hpp                | 1 +
 src/cpu_depth_packet_processor.cpp                     | 2 ++
 src/depth_packet_stream_parser.cpp                     | 6 ++++++
 src/frame_listener_impl.cpp                            | 1 +
 src/opencl_depth_packet_processor.cpp                  | 2 ++
 src/opencl_kde_depth_packet_processor.cpp              | 2 ++
 src/opengl_depth_packet_processor.cpp                  | 2 ++
 src/rgb_packet_stream_parser.cpp                       | 6 ++++++
 src/tee_jpeg_rgb_packet_processor.cpp                  | 1 +
 src/turbo_jpeg_rgb_packet_processor.cpp                | 1 +
 12 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

